-- title:
--   Invariance of Y under multiplication by qⁿ
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a nontrivially normed field whose norm satisfies the ultrametric inequality and which is complete, let $q, u \in K$ with $q \neq 0$, and let $n$ be an integer. The assertion is that `pointY q (q ^ n * u) = pointY q u`, that is, the quantity $\mathrm{pointY}$ attached to the pair $(q,u)$ — by definition the sum of the family $\big(\mathrm{yfun}(q^m u)\big)_{m \in \mathbb{Z}}$, taken as an unconditional sum over $m \in \mathbb{Z}$ (its value being $0$ when the family is not summable), plus the correction term $s_1(q)$ given by `s₁ q` — is unchanged when $u$ is replaced by $q^n u$. Thus $\mathrm{pointY}(q, \cdot)$ is invariant under the group of translations of the punctured disc generated by multiplication by $q$, for an arbitrary integer exponent $n$, positive, zero or negative; no hypothesis beyond $q \neq 0$ is imposed on $q$ or $u$ (in particular no condition $\lVert q \rVert < 1$, and no summability assumption).
--
--   This is the $q^{\mathbb{Z}}$-periodicity of the $Y$-coordinate of the Tate parametrisation, upgrading periodicity under a single multiplication by $q$ to periodicity under the whole cyclic group $q^{\mathbb{Z}}$. Together with its companion for the $X$-coordinate it is used when verifying that the pair $(\mathrm{pointX}, \mathrm{pointY})$ satisfies the Weierstrass equation of the Tate curve, as in [`TateCurve.equation_pointX_pointY_of_defectCoeff_eq_zero`](thm.html#TateCurve.equation_pointX_pointY_of_defectCoeff_eq_zero).
-- source:
